            "review_title": "Review at Thanh Phat",
            "review_text": "Pink Lys\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam142 contributions\n0\nFresh seafood, crowded and expensive\nNov 2017 • Family\nTogether with Ganh Hao, Thanh Phat is a famous seafood restaurant for tourist in Vung Tau. It take around 20 mins to drive from the city center to Thanh Phat. This restaurant locates next to a small harbor, the destination of some fish men after fishing, to sell their result; so there is no doubt that Thanh Phat have a good source for fresh seafood. However, the price is not cheap as people say. Compare to other small restaurant next to them, they are 20% higher in price.\nBeing famous, Thanh Phat is always full and crowded especially during weekend and holiday. If you want a nice and clean place for dining, this is not a choice. \nFor the food, we ordered blue crab at $22/kg, seaweed salad, small squid, fried rice and boiled vegetable with fish sauce. The crabs and fried rice are really good, squid is not as fresh as we expected, and vegetable is ok. It cost us $60 for the meal with 7 people. \nIt’s worth a recommendation, but next time, we will consider other restaurants around that.\nRead more\nWritten November 18, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-03",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
