            "review_text": "JimmyDevasia\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam223 contributions\n0\nExcellent seafood\nApr 2015\nWas taken out to dinner by a client (local).\nReached around 4 pm, so got the best seats (right next to the sea). Even somebody like me could make out that the seafood tasted better (fresher i suppose) than in Saigon. Infact, fisherfolks seemed to be coming in with fresh supplies all the time! And the place filled up quite quickly with local folks out for dinner.\nTried many shell dishes, big prawns, fish, a seafood hotpot etc etc. Came away feeling very contended and well-fed! We were 8 of us, and counting some 2 Tiger beers each, it cost us around 200k vnd (10 usd) per head!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 25, 2015",
